# m4_early: a hit before 120 ticks of history exist rewinds to tick 0. A at 30, then RIGHT
# 32..140. Since M7 the first gnat string comes at 2 s (game tick 120), too late for that, so
# the test hook debug_spray at 60 (game tick 30; it spawns a fixed set of engine bullets from
# (140, 64), among them three pellets that brake and re-aim at the ship, and checkpoints the
# history) supplies the bullets: the ship flying right meets one at update 85 (game tick 55).
# The rewind goes back to tick 0 (the spray is not input, so the replayed world has none of
# it: bullets 0 at the resume). The playback length follows the depth, (55 + 1) / 2 = 28
# frames: bug report 85..104 (20 updates), playback 105..132 (game tick 53, 51, ... 0),
# resume at update 133 with game tick 0 and rewinds 2. (Until M7: UP 32..39 and RIGHT into
# the y-40 string, hit at 84, resume at 131.)
--frames 400 --call-at "60 debug_spray" --dump-exports debug_state,debug_rewinds,debug_game_tick --at "84 debug_state == 1" --at "85 debug_state == 4" --at "85 debug_game_tick == 55" --at "85 debug_rewind_target == 0" --at "104 debug_state == 4" --at "105 debug_game_tick == 53" --at "132 debug_state == 4" --at "132 debug_game_tick == 0" --at "133 debug_state == 1" --at "133 debug_game_tick == 0" --at "133 debug_rewinds == 2" --at "133 debug_bullets == 0" --at "110 debug_history_check == 0" --at "250 debug_history_check == 0" --expect "debug_state == 1"
